==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|peine|lang=fro}},
from {{etyl|la}} {{term|poena|lang=la}},
from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ποινή||penalty, fine, bloodmoney|tr=poinē|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{legal}} [[pain|Pain]] or [[punishment]].

====Usage notes====
This is only used in common law legal contexts, as part of {{w|Law French}}, most often in the phrase {{term|peine forte et dure||strong and hard pain}}.

====Derived terms====
* [[peine forte et dure]]

